diagnostic_evidence.quote:
For $|\alpha| = 0$, we have $H^0 = L^2$ and can directly apply the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality and \Cref{l:l2_invariance} to get $\left|\<\calK f, \vphi\>\right|  \leq \| \calK f\|_{L^2} \|\vphi\|_{L^2} \leq C_2 \|f\|_{L^2} \|\vphi\|_{L^2}$ and hence
\begin{align*}
    \left\|\frac{d\nu_{\vphi}}{dx}\right\|_{H^{-1}} \leq C_2 \|\vphi\|_{L^2}
\end{align*}
for some $C_2 \geq 0$.

